# Shell scripts must always check out with LF line endings, on every
# platform including Windows. `resources/shield/shield-evaluate.sh` is a
# POSIX sh script Shield's generated hooks invoke directly (never through
# a shell that tolerates CRLF); a Windows checkout with the common
# `core.autocrlf=true` default silently converts it to CRLF, which
# breaks it in ways that are easy to misdiagnose as a logic bug rather
# than a checkout artifact -- confirmed directly: its shebang line
# checked out as `#!/bin/sh\r` on windows-latest CI, and Shield's own
# GitHub SSH account-verification decisions differed as a downstream
# effect of the same corruption. `eol=lf` forces LF on checkout
# regardless of the checking-out platform's `core.autocrlf` setting.
*.sh text eol=lf
